are' test point are consistent.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.275,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'removes an exited unowned container over the share, nothing under it (tested at 90% of the share, i.e. between the low-water mark and the ceiling)'","§Sizes and termination: 'stopping at 80% of the share' names only the stop target, not the trigger","§Alarms: 'rebar-container-writable-usage-high (>85%)' — a third distinct threshold","ABSENCE: no line states the usage level at which --reap begins acting"],"finding":"The reaper's TRIGGER threshold (the usage level at which reaping begins) is never stated, and AC line 1 contradicts itself about it: it promises reaping happens 'over the share, nothing under it' yet says it is 'tested at 90% of the share, i.e. between the low-water mark and the ceiling' — 90% of the share is BELOW the share, so either the trigger is the 80% low-water mark (not the share) or the test violates the stated guarantee. The '§Sizes and termination' prose only fixes the STOP target ('stopping at 80% of the share') and the alarm fires at 85%, leaving three thresholds (trigger, stop=80%, alarm=85%) whose relationship an implementer must guess.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faf465fc1806d4fe7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1; §Sizes and termination; §Alarms","norm_id":"n1b55fa9402a555f3","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Usage sits at 82% of the share: does --reap act (trigger ≤ 80%, already at stop target) or not (trigger = share = 100%)?","Usage at 90% of the share (the AC's own test point): the guarantee says 'nothing under [the share]' yet the test expects a removal"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the trigger as the low-water mark (reap when usage > 80% of the share, down to 80%) and rewrite AC1 to test just-above-80% (reap) and just-below-80% (no-op), or, if the trigger is the share (100%), change the AC test point to just-over-share and drop the 'between the low-water mark and the ceiling' phrasing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an AC that --check-active publishes container_reaper_active=1 when the reaper timer is active and 0 when it is inactive/absent.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0611,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC #3: \"the state metrics publish every tick including their 0 path\"","AC #5: \"Both alarms exist by name ... nothing alarms on container_quota_enforceable\"","The heartbeat's whole purpose per plan is to detect a 'silently-dead timer' — the mapping timer-dead -> container_reaper_active=0 is the load-bearing behavior"],"finding":"No acceptance criterion proves that container_reaper_active actually tracks timer state — AC #3 pins publish-on-every-tick behavior and AC #5 pins the alarm's existence, but nothing exercises the --check-active path deriving the 1 vs 0 value from an active vs inactive timer.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9899d7a7136bd203","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC #3 and AC #5)","norm_id":"nc6d5f19708c3b208","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add: `--check-active` publishes `container_reaper_active=1` for an active timer fixture and `=0` for an inactive/missing timer fixture.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concrete detection source for container_reaper_active (e.g. `systemctl is-active rebar-container-reaper.timer`) and container_quota_enforceable (e.g. the XFS pquota mount-option / project-quota check) in the plan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"container_reaper_active (is the timer in force — the heartbeat)\"","\"container_quota_enforceable (is the kernel enforcing XFS project quota on the Docker root fs)\"","Signal (1)/(2): a referenced output field with no stated source/provenance is a data-design ambiguity"],"finding":"The derivation of the two 1/0 state metrics (container_reaper_active, container_quota_enforceable) is described conceptually but no concrete detection command/source is specified — 'is the timer in force' and 'is the kernel enforcing XFS project quota' leave the actual probe (e.g. systemctl is-active, mount-option / xfs_quota check) to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcf8643cd29af2d9d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Observability (publish-or-stay-silent) section","norm_id":"n3fe8ade60127f1fe","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Name the exact command each state metric reads: container_reaper_active from the timer's active state, container_quota_enforceable from the Docker-root fs mount options / xfs_quota state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"med